  "spec_section": "protocol.md §9.5.2 (color_groups canonical JSON inside vault.prefs)",
  "description": "Pins protocol::color_group::parse_color_groups_array — the canonical-JSON decoder for the color_groups array embedded in vault.prefs (MYND-604, graph color groups). parse_ok cases pin the decoded rule-set as its canonical re-encoding (canonical_encode_color_groups — CALLER ORDER preserved VERBATIM, never id-sorted unlike saved_views, because array position IS rule precedence; plus NFC folding + lexicographic per-object key order color<enabled<filter<id<name) plus the exact consumed byte count (the cursor-advance contract the prefs decoder relies on); parse_fail cases pin the closed error surface (malformed / missing_field / wrong_type / unrepresentable — the last covers unknown filter kind + unknown comparison operator, the reused saved_view FilterNode allow-list). Cases generated by `cargo test -p protocol --lib emit_color_group_vectors_for_paste -- --ignored`.",
